  "notes": "{移|うつ}す means to move or transfer something from one place or state to another. It also has the distinct meaning of passing on an illness.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {移|うつ}る (intransitive — to move, to shift)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{移|うつ}している indicates the action of moving/transferring is in progress.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xを〜に{移|うつ}す: to move X to ~\n- {視線|しせん}を{移|うつ}す: to shift one's gaze\n- {住|す}まいを{移|うつ}す: to relocate one's home\n- {風邪|かぜ}を{移|うつ}す: to pass on a cold\n\nUSAGE:\nThe illness meaning (sense 2) uses the same kanji but is a separate usage. Be careful not to confuse with {写|うつ}す (to copy, to photograph) or {映|うつ}す (to reflect, to project).",
